.TH EXPAND "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
expand \- convert tabs to spaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expand
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Convert tabs in each FILE to spaces, writing to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#expand-i'\fB\-i, \-\-initial\fP\X'tty: link'
do not convert tabs after non blanks
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#expand-t'\fB\-t, \-\-tabs=\,N\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
have tabs N characters apart, not 8
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#expand-t'\fB\-t, \-\-tabs=\,LIST\fP\X'tty: link'\/\fR
use comma separated list of tab positions.
The last specified position can be prefixed with '/'
to specify a tab size to use after the last
explicitly specified tab stop.  Also a prefix of '+'
can be used to align remaining tab stops relative to
the last specified tab stop instead of the first column
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/expand#expand--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/expand#expand--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
